  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "There are NNN shops in the town, numbered from 111 to NNN. The iii-th shop has an infinite amount of items with value ViV_iVi​ each. And each item in each shop costs exactly 111 dollar.\n\nTo prevent you from spending all your money buying just the items of maximum value, you have to follow some rules:\n\n\n\nLet numinum_inumi​ be the number of items you bought at the iii-th store.\n\n\n\n\nnum1num_1num1​ can only be either 000 or 111.\n\n\n\n\nnumi≤numi−1+1num_i \\leq num_{i-1}+1numi​≤numi−1​+1 for 2≤i≤N2\\leq i \\leq N2≤i≤N.\n\n\n\nFind the maximum sum of value you can obtain if you can spend a total of KKK dollars.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and KKK — the number of shops and the money you have.\nThe next line contains NNN space-separated integers V1,V2,V3,...,VNV_1, V_2, V_3, ... , V_NV1​,V2​,V3​,...,VN​ - the value of the items in the NNN shops.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output a single integer - the maximum sum of value you can achive.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤N,K≤12001 \\leq N,K \\leq 12001≤N,K≤1200",
      "0≤Vi≤1090 \\leq V_i \\leq 10^90≤Vi​≤109",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask 1 (11 points):** 1≤N,K≤1001 \\leq N, K \\leq 1001≤N,K≤100",
      "**Subtask 2 (19 points):** 1≤N,K≤5001 \\leq N, K \\leq 5001≤N,K≤500, **Time limits = 2s in this Subtask**.",
      "**Subtask 3 (70 points):** No further constraints."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "5 5\n3 5 4 2 6",
        "output": "23",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThe optimal choice is to buy 111 item in the first shop, 222 in the second, 111 in the third, 000 in the fourth, and 111 in the fifth.\nThe sum of values are (1×3)+(2×5)+(1×4)+(0×2)+(1×6)=23.(1 \\times 3) + (2 \\times 5) + (1 \\times 4) + (0 \\times 2) + (1 \\times 6) = 23.(1×3)+(2×5)+(1×4)+(0×2)+(1×6)=23."
      }
    ]
  },
